--TEST--
The value `Core\Script::finish()` raises leaves through every `finally` between the call and the top of the program and through no `catch` arm at all, where an ordinary error out of the same frames is taken by one — `rule:errors/propagation`, `rule:errors/throwable-hierarchy`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Script\Finished
// One question asked of both values that travel the throw path out of the same
// three frames: which blocks run. Counting the arms that took something is what
// makes the answer an assertion rather than a plausible-looking line — an
// ending that had come to descend from `Throwable` would be caught by the arm
// below and still print a cleanup line for every level.
uint $taken = 0;

class Depth {
    public static function reach(uint $left, string $ending): void {
        try {
            if ($left == 0) {
                if ($ending == "throw") {
                    throw new RuntimeError("an ordinary error");
                }
                Core\Script::finish();
                echo "the call to finish returned\n";
                return;
            }
            Depth::reach($left - 1, $ending);
        } finally {
            echo "cleanup at level ", $left, "\n";
        }
    }
}

// An ordinary error out of three frames: every `finally` runs on the way out,
// and the arm at the top takes it.
try {
    Depth::reach(3, "throw");
} catch (Throwable $ordinary) {
    $taken = $taken + 1;
    echo "an arm took ", $ordinary->message, "\n";
}

// The ending out of the same three frames. Every `finally` runs again, so the
// script leaves the way a throw does; the arm takes nothing, so what it leaves
// with is not an error. The count is printed from a `finally`, which is the
// only kind of block still running once the script has ended.
try {
    Depth::reach(3, "finish");
    echo "back at the top\n";
} catch (Throwable $anything) {
    $taken = $taken + 1;
    echo "an arm took the ending\n";
} finally {
    echo "arms that took something: ", $taken, "\n";
}

echo "the end of the script\n";
--EXPECT--
cleanup at level 0
cleanup at level 1
cleanup at level 2
cleanup at level 3
an arm took an ordinary error
cleanup at level 0
cleanup at level 1
cleanup at level 2
cleanup at level 3
arms that took something: 1
